.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD-GC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd-gc
.Nd ocifbsd garbage collection daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fvh
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon performs periodic garbage collection for the
.Xr ocifbsd 8
OCI runtime.
It scans container, image, volume, and network state on disk
and the host's network and ZFS configuration to identify and
remove resources that are orphaned, stopped past their
time-to-live, or no longer referenced.
.Pp
Collection passes are scheduled on a configurable interval
(see
.Pa /etc/ocifbsd/ocifbsd.conf )
and cover:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Orphaned container jails (no owner record).
.It
Stopped containers older than the stopped-container TTL.
.It
Finished pods older than the container TTL.
.It
Unused OCI images older than the image TTL, or when image
storage usage crosses the configured high/low watermarks.
.It
Pinned images are never collected.
.It
Orphaned volumes and released PersistentVolumeClaims.
.It
Orphaned and unused bridge networks.
.It
Dead-node resources in clustered deployments.
.It
Stale node registrations.
.El
.Pp
Deletions are delegated back to the main
.Xr ocifbsd 8
binary via
.Xr execvp 3
when a resource needs to be removed, so all cleanup honours
the runtime's safety checks and audit logging.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground.
The default is to daemonize via
.Xr daemon 3 .
.It Fl v
Enable verbose syslog output for every GC item considered.
.It Fl h
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.El
.Pp
The daemon handles
.Dv SIGTERM ,
.Dv SIGINT ,
and
.Dv SIGHUP
for graceful shutdown.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/ocifbsd -compact
.It Pa /var/run/ocifbsd
Default state directory used for container, image, volume,
and network metadata (
.Pa OCIFBSD_STATE_DIR
in the source).
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/images
Default image storage directory
.Pq Dq OCIFBSD_IMAGE_DIR .
.It Pa /usr/sbin/ocifbsd
Path to the main
.Xr ocifbsd 8
binary invoked for delete operations
.Pq Dq OCIFBSD_BIN .
.It Pa tank/ocifbsd
Default ZFS dataset for container roots
.Pq Dq OCIFBSD_ZFS_POOL .
.It Pa /etc/ocifbsd/ocifbsd.conf
Runtime configuration (intervals, TTLs, watermarks).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ocifbsd 8 ,
.Xr daemon 3 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr pfctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility was developed by
